  "name": "Terrorize",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-eye.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Fear sparks within the heart of your enemies, causing them to lose their nerve. You can spend an action and expend one link depth from the link of a linked creature to cause that creature to become frightened of you. You are immune to all damage originating from the creature while they are frightened in this way. They can end the condition at the start of their turn by ending their turn, or by passing a wisdom saving throw at the end of their turn after taking their turn normally.</p><p><a href=\"https://dnd-wiki.org/wiki/Empath_(5e_Class)\">Source: Empath by Axis, co-authored by Ghostwheel</a> (CC BY-SA 3.0). See the module's AUTOMATION.md for what is automated and how rules are interpreted.</p>",
